    {
      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "contentPreview": "WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND ONE BRANCH: this is why the CLI escapes the MCP write-validation bounds (MaxPathLength / MaxContentBytesPerElement in MemoryTools.cs:97-98) -- design review 2026-08-16 finding on validation having three homes. Any branch that adds a rule \u0027at the MCP surface\u0027 must decide explicitly whether the CLI gets it, and adding it only to the facade silently exempts every \u0060scri\u0060 command. Relevant to review branches 6 (published surface coherence) and 7.",
